                <pb facs="0258" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg186"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Fletcher to
                        the Prince of Ching.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-07-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Imperial Highness</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inform Your Highness that I have been directed by the President of the United
                    States to convey through Your Highness’s board to His Imperial Highness the
                    Prince Regent the President’s high appreciation of the prompt action of His
                    Imperial Highness the Prince Regent in instructing that arrangements be made
                    through the American chargé d’affaires for equal participation of American
                    capital in the pending railway loan, as requested by the President in his
                    telegram to the Prince Regent of July 15. The President especially appreciates
                    the cordial spirit of His Imperial Highness’s message.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                    Fletcher.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
